{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48325-who-is-a-demon-who-is-an-angel","id":48325,"title":"Who is a Demon, Who is an Angel ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-13T11:07:51-08:00","id":48325,"title":"Who is a Demon, Who is an Angel ?","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm reading the Demon book, and a question is bothering me, and I can't find the answer.<br /> <br /> How can a Demon tel someone else (under cover) is a Demon or an Angel ?<br /> <br /> Is there some kind of mechanics like in Vampire (Predator taint) ?<br /> Or is doesn't know, and just by putting things together does he suspect someone to be a Demon or an Angel ?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your insight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/703-13th-hour","name":"13th Hour","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar703_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:20:10-08:00","id":48337,"title":"","content":"Aetheric Resonance should have the answers you're looking for... basically Demons can spend a point of aether to send out a ping to reach out to other Demons in a given area. As for Angels, Demons are able to sense when a angel uses their powers, and absorb some aether from it... Don't have access to the pdf here, otherwise I'd give you a better answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:28:18-08:00","id":48347,"title":"","content":"The answer is what I was looking for. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/703-13th-hour","name":"13th Hour","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar703_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T17:41:12-08:00","id":48614,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, Aetheric Resonance doesn't immediately pierce demonic cover or angelic concealment infrastructure, so unless they spend essence or aether, you really can't tell who they are just by activating it (which does expose <i>you</i>, by the way).<br /> <br /> This is intentional. They wanted to build in paranoia and trust issues into the daily life of the Unchained, and making it so you can't tell if the person you're talking to comes from the God-Machine, and if they <i>are</i>, you can't tell if they're an angel or a demon.<br /> <br /> (Well, actually it's pretty easy to tell that last bit, but theoretically it's supposed to be a lot harder than it is in practice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T20:43:03-08:00","id":48693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48325-who-is-a-demon-who-is-an-angel?p=48614#post48614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind, Aetheric Resonance doesn't immediately pierce demonic cover or angelic concealment infrastructure, so unless they spend essence or aether, you really can't tell who they are just by activating it (which does expose <i>you</i>, by the way).<br /> <br /> This is intentional. They wanted to build in paranoia and trust issues into the daily life of the Unchained, and making it so you can't tell if the person you're talking to comes from the God-Machine, and if they <i>are</i>, you can't tell if they're an angel or a demon.<br /> <br /> (Well, actually it's pretty easy to tell that last bit, but theoretically it's supposed to be a lot harder than it is in practice.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I found that my players were more cautious than they otherwise have been while we were playing Demon. They actually exchanged nervous glances when they used Aetheric Resonance and it pinged, or if they suspected that someone they were dealing with was a demon or angel (but they couldn't tell for sure).<br /> <br /> It really brings the paranoia to the fore, which I think is a good thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T22:03:30-08:00","id":49563,"title":"","content":"The only thing that could tell you that someone is a demon is that he reacts to an aetheric resonance ping.....but then again demons only do what they WANT to do and have no visible nervous reactions if they dont want to so could be that even a demon sits still while being pinged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:47:52-08:00","id":49838,"title":"","content":"How this creates a certain paranoia is one of my favorite things about playing Demon at the moment and what I am most excited about my future Demon game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}